{"id":"st2110-10","designation":"ST 2110-10","title":"Professional Media Over Managed IP Networks — System Timing and Definitions","state":"active","suite":"2110","official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/st2110-10/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/st2110-10/","checked_at":"2026-11-18"},"scope":"This standard is part of a family of engineering documents that define an extensible system of RTP-based essence streams referenced to a common reference clock, in a manner which specifies their timing relationships. This standard specifies the system timing model and the requirements common to all of the essence streams, and defines timestamping methods for video streams and audio streams such that time alignment across essence is possible.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"1 Scope","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"2 Conformance Notation","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"3 Normative References","page":5},{"level":1,"title":"4 Terms and Definitions","page":6},{"level":1,"title":"5 Textual Conventions","page":8},{"level":2,"title":"5.1 SDP Parameters and Values","page":8},{"level":1,"title":"6 Network Interface Requirements","page":8},{"level":2,"title":"6.1 General Requirements","page":8},{"level":2,"title":"6.2 Real-Time Transport Protocol (RTP)","page":8},{"level":2,"title":"6.3 Standard UDP Size Limit","page":9},{"level":2,"title":"6.4 Extended UDP Size Limit","page":9},{"level":2,"title":"6.5 Unicast and Multicast","page":9},{"level":1,"title":"7 System Timing Model","page":9},{"level":2,"title":"7.1 Introduction to the System Timing Model (informative)","page":9},{"level":2,"title":"7.2 Distribution of the Common Reference Clock via PTP","page":10},{"level":2,"title":"7.3 RTP Clock Offset","page":10},{"level":2,"title":"7.4 RTP Clock and Media Clock","page":10},{"level":2,"title":"7.5 RTP Timestamps – General Provisions","page":11},{"level":2,"title":"7.6 RTP Timestamps for Video Streams","page":11},{"level":3,"title":"7.6.1 Video RTP Timestamps - General",